    "created_at": "2024-08-30T16:57:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-08-30T16:57:37Z",
    "body": "Oh I like that proposal a lot - that interacts much better with a future where one can open dialogs declaratively from HTML, like we support for popover now.\r\n\r\nIf that @mfreed7 is going to work on that issue, then I'm happy to have that be the solution for this problem :)\r\n\r\nMaybe we can simplify that proposal by initially only doing `closedby=\"none\"` and `closedby=\"closerequest\" as a first pass? That allows us to do the backdrop click close machinery as a follow up.\r\n\r\n(Also I think this should be called `autocloseby`, because `closeby=\"none\"` is backwards with the fact that you can still call `dialog.close()`.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
